course: dictionary
lesson: 10213
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you need context to know which one the writer means. Read «Titan is Saturn's biggest moon, larger than the planet Mercury.» The clues biggest and larger tell you that titan here means something huge.
explain: Titan can also describe a person. In «a titan of industry», the words of industry tell you the meaning is about work and business. A titan there is a very big, strong or important person, not a giant from a story.
explain: A capital letter is another clue. Titan with a capital T is often a name, like the moon Titan. Titans with a capital T in Greek myths were giant gods, so look at the rest of the sentence to decide which meaning fits.
fact: A titan is a person or thing that is very big, strong or important.
fact: The Titans were giant, powerful gods in Greek myths who ruled before Zeus and the Olympian gods defeated them.
fact: Titan is the largest moon of the planet Saturn, and the only moon with a thick atmosphere.
fact: NASA's Dragonfly is planned to fly in the thick air of Titan in the 2030s.
fact: Context clues, like «biggest» and «larger», help you choose the right meaning of a word.
exercise: «Titan is Saturn's biggest moon, larger than the planet Mercury.» What is Titan in this sentence? | *A moon of Saturn | A giant god from myth | A kind of rain | A ship that sank long ago
exercise: «She is a titan of industry, who built factories all over the country.» What does titan mean here? | A type of rain | A ship | *A very big, strong or important person | A giant god from myth
exercise: «On Titan the rain is natural gas falling as liquid, filling lakes you could sail a boat on.» What does this tell you about Titan's lakes? | *They are big enough to sail a boat on | They are dry all year | They are made of water | They are small puddles
test: Titan is a moon of which planet? | Mercury | Jupiter | *Saturn | Mars
test: Priya reads that the Titans ruled before Zeus. What were the Titans in Greek myths? | *Giant, powerful gods | A kind of rain | Lakes on a moon | Explorers on Saturn
exam: What is the best clue that Titan is huge? | Titan is a moon | *It is larger than the planet Mercury | Its name starts with a capital T | It is near Saturn
